msgid "§0"
msgstr ""

#: Game/Levels/LeanBasics/L05_Exists.lean:5
msgid "There exists"
msgstr ""

#. §0: `∃ x, …`
#. §1: `∃ x : ℝ, x + 1 = 5`
#. §2: `use 4`
#. §3: `4`
#. §4: `x`
#. §5: `4 + 1 = 5`
#. §6: `norm_num`
#. §7: `∃`
#. §8: `\\ex`
#. §9: `∀`
#. §10: `\\all`
#: Game/Levels/LeanBasics/L05_Exists.lean:7
msgid "\"Solve this equation\" is often the goal §0. Prove it by naming a solution.\n"
"For example, for §1 you would write §2: Lean puts §3 in place of\n"
"§4 and leaves you to check §5 (which §6 does).\n"
"\n"
"**Typing:** §7 is §8, §9 is §10."
msgstr ""

#. §0: $x$
#. §1: $2x = 6$
#: Game/Levels/LeanBasics/L05_Exists.lean:15
msgid "There is a real number §0 with §1."
msgstr ""

#. §0: $x$
#. §1: $2x = 6$
#. §2: `use`
#: Game/Levels/LeanBasics/L05_Exists.lean:17
msgid "Which number §0 satisfies §1? Then §2 it."
msgstr ""

#: Game/Levels/LeanBasics/L05_Exists.lean:19
msgid "Now check the arithmetic."
msgstr ""

#: Game/Levels/LeanBasics/L05_Exists.lean:23
msgid "Many \"find the solution\" questions on the sheets look like this: you supply\n"
"the witness, Lean checks it."
msgstr ""

#: Game/Levels/LeanBasics/L06_Not.lean:5
msgid "Not"
msgstr ""

#. §0: `¬ P`
#. §1: `intro hp`
#. §2: `P`
#. §3: `False`
#. §4: `1 = 2`
#. §5: `False`
#. §6: `norm_num at h`
#. §7: `intro`
#. §8: `intro h`
#. §9: `h`
#. §10: `h`
#. §11: `¬`
#. §12: `\\not`
#. §13: `≠`
#. §14: `\\ne`
#: Game/Levels/LeanBasics/L06_Not.lean:7
msgid "§0 means \"P leads to a contradiction\". To prove it, §1 assumes §2; your goal\n"
"becomes §3. A hypothesis like §4 gives you §5 via §6.\n"
"\n"
"**Names matter.** When you §7 something, give it a *new* name. If you reuse a name\n"
"that is already taken (say §8 when there is already an §9), the old §10 is hidden:\n"
"it is shown with a † and you can no longer refer to it. If that happens, press Retry and\n"
"pick a fresh name.\n"
"\n"
"**Typing:** §11 is §12, §13 is §14."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `x ≠ 2`
#. §1: `¬ (x = 2)`
#. §2: `x = 2`
#. §3: `«{h}»`
#. §4: `intro h2`
#: Game/Levels/LeanBasics/L06_Not.lean:21
msgid "§0 means §1. Assume §2 and give the assumption a *new* name\n"
"(not §3, which is taken), for example §4."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `x`
#. §1: `«{h2}»`
#. §2: `rw [«{h}»] at «{h2}»`
#: Game/Levels/LeanBasics/L06_Not.lean:24
msgid "Substitute what you know about §0 into §1: §2."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `«{h2}»`
#. §1: `1 = 2`
#. §2: `norm_num at «{h2}»`
#: Game/Levels/LeanBasics/L06_Not.lean:26
msgid "§0 now claims §1. §2 sees that it is false."
msgstr ""

#: Game/Levels/LeanBasics/L07_Or.lean:5
msgid "Or, and case splits"
msgstr ""

#. §0: `P ∨ Q`
#. §1: `left`
#. §2: `P`
#. §3: `right`
#. §4: `Q`
#. §5: `h : P ∨ Q`
#. §6: `rcases h with hp | hq`
#. §7: `hp : P`
#. §8: `hq : Q`
#. §9: `∨`
#. §10: `\\or`
#. §11: `|`
#: Game/Levels/LeanBasics/L07_Or.lean:7
msgid "Two moves with \"or\":\n"
"- To *prove* §0, pick the side you can prove: §1 turns the goal into §2,\n"
"  §3 turns it into §4.\n"
"- To *use* §5, split into two cases with §6. You then get\n"
"  **two goals** (two tabs): the first where §7 holds, the second where §8\n"
"  holds. Each still has the original goal, and you prove it once per case.\n"
"\n"
"**Typing:** §9 is §10; the bar §11 is on your keyboard."
msgstr ""

#. §0: $x = 1$
#. §1: $x = 2$
#. §2: $x \\cdot x = 1$
#. §3: $x \\cdot x = 4$
#: Game/Levels/LeanBasics/L07_Or.lean:18
msgid "If §0 or §1, then §2 or §3."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `«{h}»`
#. §1: `rcases «{h}» with h1 | h2`
#: Game/Levels/LeanBasics/L07_Or.lean:20
msgid "Split on §0: §1."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `«{h1}» : x = 1`
#. §1: $x = 1$
#: Game/Levels/LeanBasics/L07_Or.lean:22
msgid "This is the case §0 (the other case is in the next tab). The goal is\n"
"still an \"or\": which side is true when §1?"
msgstr ""

#. §0: $1 \\cdot 1 = 1$
#. §1: `left`
#. §2: `rw [«{h1}»]`
#. §3: `norm_num`
#: Game/Levels/LeanBasics/L07_Or.lean:24
msgid "§0, so the left side. §1, then §2, then §3."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `«{h2}» : x = 2`
#: Game/Levels/LeanBasics/L07_Or.lean:28
msgid "Now the case §0. Which side is true now?"
msgstr ""

#. §0: `right`
#. §1: `rw [«{h2}»]`
#. §2: `norm_num`
#: Game/Levels/LeanBasics/L07_Or.lean:29
#: Game/Levels/Isomorphisms/L02_InverseLinear.lean:35
msgid "§0, then §1, then §2."
msgstr ""

#: Game/Levels/LeanBasics/L08_Components.lean:5
msgid "Vectors: components"
msgstr ""

#. §0: $\\mathbb R^n$
#. §1: `![3, 7]`
#. §2: $\\begin{pmatrix}3\\\\7\\end{pmatrix}$
#. §3: $\\mathbb R^2$
#. §4: `v 0`
#. §5: `v 1`
#. §6: `norm_num`
#: Game/Levels/LeanBasics/L08_Components.lean:7
msgid "In this game a vector in §0 is written with square brackets after an\n"
"exclamation mark: §1 is the vector §2 in §3.\n"
"\n"
"A vector is really a *function* from positions to numbers, so §4 is its first entry and\n"
"§5 its second. **Positions are numbered from 0.**\n"
"\n"
"§6 can read off an entry of a vector written out like this."
msgstr ""

#. §0: $(3, 7)$
#. §1: $7$
#: Game/Levels/LeanBasics/L08_Components.lean:17
msgid "The second entry of §0 is §1."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `1`
#: Game/Levels/LeanBasics/L08_Components.lean:19
msgid "Position §0 is the *second* entry. The calculator can evaluate it."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `Fin 2`
#. §1: $\\{0, 1\\}$
#. §2: `Fin 2 → ℝ`
#. §3: $\\mathbb R^2$
#: Game/Levels/LeanBasics/L08_Components.lean:23
msgid "§0 is the set of positions §1, and §2 is §3."
msgstr ""

#: Game/Levels/LeanBasics/L09_VectorEq.lean:5
msgid "Vectors: equal entry by entry"
msgstr ""

#. §0: `entrywise`
#. §1: `u = v`
#. §2: `u 0 = v 0`
#. §3: `u 1 = v 1`
#. §4: `entrywise`
#. §5: `ext i`
#. §6: `fin_cases i`
#. §7: `ext`
#. §8: `i`
#. §9: `fin_cases i`
#: Game/Levels/LeanBasics/L09_VectorEq.lean:7
msgid "Two vectors are equal when they agree in every position. The tactic §0 turns\n"
"§1 into one goal per position — §2, §3, … — shown as tabs.\n"
"\n"
"(Under the hood, §4 is §5 followed by §6 — two tactics you will also use on their own later: §7 reduces an equation of vectors to one entry §8, and §9 splits into the possible positions.)"
msgstr ""

